---
# What a test does that the library must not, each the same in every test:
# readability-magic-numbers: a test's numbers are its data, 7 or 20, which
#   read better as the numbers they are than behind names used once.
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast: a test makes chars in flash as
#   F() of the core does, by a cast, to hand them to the library.
# cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables: a free function that a
#   test binds reaches what it counts or changes only through a global.
# readability-function-size.LineThreshold: a test of many cases is long but
#   flat; its parameters, nesting and complexity keep the library's limits.
# readability-function-cognitive-complexity.IgnoreMacros: GoogleTest's
#   EXPECT_ and ASSERT_ expand to an if and an else each, so a test without a
#   branch of its own counted 20; its own branches still count.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables
CheckOptions:
  readability-function-size.LineThreshold: none
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.IgnoreMacros: true
